# Pure-fact data (non-negotiable)

Production tennis data is **facts from Tennis API only**. If the provider does not prove it, MatchRead does not store or show it.

## Allowed

- Tournament rows with a real `provider_tournament_id` (calendar metadata is ok before a draw exists)
- Draw seats where every **non-bye** has `provider_player_id` + a real last name
- Byes: `is_bye = true`, `provider_player_id` null
- Match results / schedule whose `winner_ref` / `match_key` map to those seats
- Pre-draw public pages: name, dates, tour, surface, countdown — **no empty or invented bracket**

## Forbidden

- Fictional seats (`Player47`, `p-0`…`p-15`, `Player ${id}`)
- Opening `/enter` or “draw open” without verified provider seats
- Reconstructing a partial draw (e.g. 20 of 32 first-round matches) to look complete
- Guessing bracket order, seeds, or byes the provider did not prove
- Hard-coding tournament URLs/refs instead of reading `tournaments.ref`
- Odds, predictions, or any non-fact product data

## If the API is incomplete

Keep the event **draw pending**. Fail closed. Do not wipe a verified draw to fill a gap with fiction. Do not ship a showcase/fixture draw on the live calendar.

```sql
-- A public draw is verified only when this is true:
-- non-bye seats > 0 AND every non-bye has provider_player_id
```
